# Daily SEO agent

Goal: make https://www.kavehrs.com a Persian **reference for notes about software and technology** (programming, Linux, monitoring, tools, and related personal notes). Climb reports rank on https://logbook.rocks, not here.

## When this applies

- Scheduled daily SEO automation
- **45-minute SEO + AI-source watch** (`.cursor/skills/seo-ai-source-watch/SKILL.md`)
- Any request to audit, improve, or update site SEO or AI citation / source listing

## Required workflow

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/skills/daily-seo-audit/SKILL.md`.
2. Pull latest authoritative SEO guidance (Google Search Central, Bing Webmaster Guidelines, schema.org) before changing markup.
3. Audit the live site and the repo (meta, canonical, sitemap, robots, structured data, internal links, images, Core Web Vitals proxies, crawl errors).
4. Implement only evidence-based improvements; keep PRs narrowly scoped.
5. Run `bundle exec jekyll build` and confirm `_drafts/` / `.cursor/` are not published.
6. Open PR, then merge after a clean build when the change is high-confidence.

## Ranking priorities (software / technology notes)

1. Unique technical notes (`note_kind: technical`) with clear titles/descriptions — hub `/tech/`
2. Structured data (`BlogPosting`) and hub CollectionPage on `/tech/` and `/notes/`
3. Internal links between related notes of the same `note_kind`
4. Accurate Open Graph / Twitter images when the note has a real cover
5. Technical hygiene: broken links, missing alts, wrong `lang`/`dir`, sitemap noise
6. `/logbook/*` stays a redirect to logbook.rocks — do not put report bodies back on this site

## Notes content (this site)

When touching `_blog/` during SEO work:

- do not rewrite published bodies unless the owner asked to edit that file
- keep `note_kind: personal` vs `technical`; hubs `/notes/` and `/tech/`
- related UI stays a flat `یادداشت‌های مرتبط :` list
- reader-facing dates stay Jalali (`_includes/jalali-date.html`)
- never publish agent/implementation notes into live page copy
- do not keyword-stuff software/technology terms into unrelated personal notes

## 45-minute SEO + AI-source watch

Cadence: every 45 minutes until the owner pauses it. Watch **official** SEO docs and AI-citation materials (`_seo/guidance-sources.yml`), then apply **technical** site signals only (`robots.txt`, `/llms.txt`, WebMCP, IndexNow, `rel=describedby`, crawl headers).

This is not a Google rank refresh.

**Never edit existing `_blog/*.md` bodies, titles, descriptions, tags, or `note_kind`** on this watch. Research notes go in unpublished `_seo/watch-inbox.md`.

## Hard limits

- Do not rewrite published note copy to chase SEO or AI citations.
- Do not keyword-stuff titles or body copy.
- Do not republish climb reports on this site.
- Do not remove `noindex` from archive/projects/404 without explicit user request.
- Do not change analytics IDs or domain/`CNAME` casually.
